1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,820
Do you ever think:

2
00:00:00,820 --> 00:00:03,290
if people really knew me,

3
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:04,670
they would leave?

4
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:09,490
One night, Jesus sat at supper with His closest friends.

5
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:11,090
And He knew them.

6
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:14,790
He knew one of them, Judas, would betray Him.

7
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:16,550
He knew another,

8
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:19,370
Peter, would say three times before morning:

9
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:21,010
I do not know Him.

10
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:24,180
So what does He do with friends like that?

11
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:26,730
He gets up from the table.

12
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:29,470
He ties a towel around Himself.

13
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:31,950
He pours water into a bowl,

14
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:33,670
and He washes their feet.

15
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:35,590
A servant's work.

16
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,270
And Judas is still in the room.

17
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:40,970
"Know ye what I have done to you?"

18
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:43,270
The story says it in one line:

19
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:45,830
"he loved them unto the end."

20
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:49,480
And the next day, He would die on a cross,

21
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:50,730
for them.

22
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:54,370
Later that night, Judas walks out.

23
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:57,010
And the story adds four small words:

24
00:00:58,140 --> 00:00:59,110
"and it was night."

25
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:01,830
Maybe it is night where you are.

26
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:05,550
Maybe you are sure nobody would stay, if they knew.

27
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:07,790
Jesus knows.

28
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:09,270
All of it.

29
00:01:10,140 --> 00:01:11,450
And look at that room again.

30
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:13,840
The one who knew the worst about them

31
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:15,230
was not the one who left.

32
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:18,290
He was the one holding the towel.
